🟦 EPIC 1: Historical Performance Intelligence Engine
US-01
Summary:
View Year-over-Year performance for all historical years

Description:
As an Investment Manager, I want to view YoY % performance for each year in the dataset, so that I can compare growth across different market cycles and identify the strongest and weakest performing years at a glance.

Acceptance Criteria:

YoY % change is calculated for every year in the 4,175-day dataset
Calculation uses SQL window function (LAG) for accuracy
Power BI YoY values match PostgreSQL validation query output
2017 (+605%) and 2022 (−41%) display correctly as benchmark years
Story Points: 5
Priority: High
Epic Link: Historical Performance Intelligence Engine

US-02
Summary:
Filter dashboard by specific year or period

Description:
As a Portfolio Manager, I want to filter performance data by a specific year or period, so that I can analyze isolated market phases without needing to view the entire dataset at once.

Acceptance Criteria:

Year filter/slicer is available on all dashboard pages
Filtering does not break any visuals or KPI cards
Selected year updates all relevant charts simultaneously
Story Points: 3
Priority: Medium
Epic Link: Historical Performance Intelligence Engine

🟦 EPIC 2: Investment Risk Identification Framework
US-03
Summary:
Auto-flag years exceeding ±30% YoY volatility

Description:
As a Risk Analyst, I want years exceeding ±30% YoY volatility to be automatically flagged, so that I can proactively review high-risk periods without manually scanning raw data every time.

Acceptance Criteria:

±30% YoY threshold rule is applied across the full dataset
Flagged years are visually distinct (e.g., color-coded red)
2022 (−41% YoY) is correctly flagged as high-risk
Rule applies consistently regardless of active filters
Story Points: 5
Priority: High
Epic Link: Investment Risk Identification Framework

US-04
Summary:
Highlight the single highest-risk year

Description:
As an Executive, I want the single highest-risk year clearly highlighted in the dashboard, so that I can quickly benchmark future risk events against the worst historical case.

Acceptance Criteria:

2022 is explicitly labeled as the highest-risk year (−41% YoY)
This finding is visible on the Risk Analysis page and Executive Summary page
Label updates automatically if underlying data changes
Story Points: 2
Priority: Medium
Epic Link: Investment Risk Identification Framework

🟦 EPIC 3: Market Cycle Intelligence & Strategic Context
US-05
Summary:
Document and visualize the 4-year market cycle pattern

Description:
As a member of the Executive Team, I want the 4-year market cycle pattern clearly documented and visualized, so that I can understand macro growth and correction phases without needing to interpret raw price data myself.

Acceptance Criteria:

Cycle 1 (2014–2017), Cycle 2 (2018–2022), and Cycle 3 (2023–2026) are clearly labeled
Cycle boundaries are visually distinguishable on the price trend chart
Cycle narrative is included in the Executive Summary page
Story Points: 5
Priority: Medium
Epic Link: Market Cycle Intelligence & Strategic Context

US-06
Summary:
Deliver plain-language investment recommendation

Description:
As a Retail Investor, I want a plain-language recommendation summarizing key findings, so that I don't need to interpret raw YoY percentages or technical charts myself before making a decision.

Acceptance Criteria:

Executive Summary includes a stated entry-pattern reference (+200% YoY)
Executive Summary includes a stated risk-review trigger (−30% YoY)
A disclaimer is included stating this is not financial advice
Summary is understandable to a non-technical reader
Story Points: 3
Priority: Medium
Epic Link: Market Cycle Intelligence & Strategic Context

